// # M.5 Derivation [DERIVATION]
//
//   Template lineage and inheritance.
//   Traces where this file came from in the template chain.
//
//   Derives_from: [path/to/parent/template] — file lineage (pragma meta.from = spec)
//
// Derives_from: ROOT — anchor template (pragma meta.from traces to OmniCode spec)
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.6 Classification [CLASSIFICATION]
//
//   Keywords for discovery and categorization.
//   How to find this file when searching the codebase.
//
//   Tags: [keyword, keyword, ...] — discovery and categorization
//
// Tags: config, jsonc, 3block, template, root, seed, bereshit
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.7 Intent [INTENT]
//
//   Why this file exists and what it enables.
//   The purpose, design philosophy, and key capabilities.
//
//   Purpose:     [Enables X for Y]
//   Core Design: [Architectural pattern]
//   Philosophy:  [Guiding principle]
//   Key Features:
//     - [Major capability]
//
// Purpose: Define configuration settings — structured key-value data with comments
// Core Design: JSONC format — JSON with comments for documentation
// Philosophy: Configuration as code — version controlled, documented, validated
//
// Key Features:
//   Settings:   Key-value pairs organized by category
//   Comments:   Inline documentation explaining each setting
//   Validation: Schema-compatible structure for validation tools
//   Versioning: Version-controlled configuration changes
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.8 Grounding [GROUNDING]
//
//   Biblical foundation for this file's purpose.
//   Dig deeper — find the verse that best fits THIS file's specific content.
//   Avoid common/generic verses; engage with Scripture purposefully.
//
//   Scripture: [Book Chapter:Verse] ([KJV|WEB])
//     "[text]"
//   Principle: [Kingdom principle — bridge between Scripture and purpose]
//   Anchor: [Book Chapter:Verse] ([KJV|WEB])
//     "[text]"
//
// Scripture: 2 Timothy 2:15 (WEB)
//   "Give diligence to present yourself approved by God, a workman who doesn't
//    need to be ashamed, properly handling the Word of truth."
//
// Principle: Configuration files are the foundation that systems build upon.
//   "Properly handling" means every setting documented, organized, and validated.
//   Excellence in configuration enables excellence in execution.
//
// Anchor: Proverbs 24:27 (KJV)
//   "Prepare thy work without, and make it fit for thyself in the field;
//    and afterwards build thine house."
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.9 Dependencies [DEPENDENCIES]
//
//   What this file needs and what uses it.
//   System requirements, integrations, and consumers.
//
//   What This Needs:
//     System:   [tools, parsers]
//     External: [None | dependencies]
//     Internal: [project files]
//
//   What Uses This:
//     Commands:  [functions that consume this]
//     Processes: [workflows]
//
//   Integration:
//     - [How consumers interact with this file]
//
//   [Custom]: (file-specific extensions — must align with M.8 Grounding)
//
// What This Needs:
//   System:   JSONC parser (or JSON parser that ignores comments)
//   External: None
//   Internal: None — standalone configuration
//
// What Uses This:
//   Commands:  Application that consumes config
//   Processes: Build, runtime, development workflows
//
// Integration:
//   - JSONC parsed at startup or build time
//   - Settings applied to application behavior
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.10 Roadmap [ROADMAP]
//
//   Past, present, and future of this file.
//   History of changes, current state, and planned additions.
//
//   History: [Past changes — version notes]
//   Current: [What this file provides now]
//   Planned: [Future additions]
//
// History:
//   a-01.00: Initial template creation
